text	I compared the letter with the 3 open issues in `acme/shop`. Points 2 and 3 match. Point 1 conflicts with #12. I changed nothing on GitHub.  ## 1. New partner rate: the letter conflicts with #12  - **The letter:** a new rate applies only to customers that the partner brings after the change. Commissions on current customers stay as they are. - **#12:** shows the merchant a dialog with two options. The default is **All customers**, so current customers pay the new rate from their next payment. "New customers only" is the other option. Its acceptance test checks the default: 3 customers at 5% go to 7%. - **What #12 is based on:** it says that on 29 Oct you decided to follow the market (new rate for all customers). It says that with the dialog, "the client no longer has to answer our question 1 of 23 Oct." The client answered it the next day, 30 Oct, and chose the opposite.  So #12's default, and maybe the dialog itself, goes against the client's answer. You need to decide one of these: - **(a) Follow the client.** New rate for new customers only, with no dialog. - **(b) Keep the dialog but change the default** to "New customers only." - **(c) Keep #12 as it is** and explain the reason to the client.  After you decide, #12's title, reason and acceptance test need to be rewritten. I can do that.  ## 2. Payouts: matches #13  The letter says payouts stay monthly, on the 5th. #13 says the same: "Partners are paid monthly, on the 5th." Nothing to change.  ## 3. Rate history: only partly covered  The letter asks to see **each** change of a partner's rate in the partner's history. Only #12 mentions history, and only to record which dialog option the merchant chose. No issue says that every rate change goes into the history. If you choose option (a), that line goes away with the dialog, and no issue covers the request at all. This request probably needs its own issue, or an explicit line in #12.  ## Not in the letter  #14 (CSV export of monthly commissions) has nothing in the letter that supports it or conflicts with it.
