text	Here is a draft that follows your current leaning: by default, a new rate applies to new customers only, and the merchant can still choose to apply it to all customers.  > **Change of a partner's rate.** Thank you for your answer. We will do it as you describe: by default, a new rate applies only to the customers that the partner brings after the change, and the commissions on the current customers stay as they are. When you change a rate, you will also be able to apply it to the current customers, from their next payment, if you ever need to. Each change of a partner's rate, with its date and its scope (new customers only, or all customers), will be shown in the partner's history.  The team should decide two things:  - **Keep the "all customers" option or not.** If the team chooses new customers only, with no option, delete the third sentence. Also change "(new customers only, or all customers)" to "the old rate and the new rate." - **"From their next payment."** I took this from #12. Check that this is the behaviour you want if the option stays.  I did not change #12, because you have not decided yet. When the team decides, tell me the result and I will rewrite its title, reason and acceptance test. If the history request still has no issue of its own then, I will file one.
